<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Fig. 5</span>: </span><span id="S5.F5.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
<span id="S5.F5.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Effect of Fine-Tuning on Compilation and Validation Rates.</span>
Compilation and validation rates for the LLaMA model across translation directions before and after fine-tuning. While compilation rate improvements are modest, fine-tuning substantially increases the proportion of functionally-correct outputs, with average validation rates more than doubling.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
